WEBVTT

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.830
Guys! It's coming into view!

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.830
Wow!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.830
So that's Planet Vilavurs.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.000
I'm so excited!

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.870
I wonder what kind of food we'll find!

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.330
Oh no, I forgot my sunscreen.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.160
Check this out, I made a bug net!

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.660
Cool! Let's catch some beetles!

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.080
Seriously, can you guys
be any less cautious?!

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:41.910
Cool!

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.950
--Let's make our beetles fight each other!

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.830
--Team B5, camp log. First planet, Vilavurs.
--Let's make our beetles fight each other!

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.250
--Team B5, camp log. First planet, Vilavurs.
--Interesting!

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.500
--Team B5, camp log. First planet, Vilavurs.
--Prepare to face the master beetle trainer!

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.580
--We must find and store 20 days' worth
of food and water on this planet.
--Prepare to face the master beetle trainer!

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.120
--We must find and store 20 days' worth
of food and water on this planet.
--Wonderful! Let's add stag beetles to the mix.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.120
--Cool!
--Stag beetles!

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.950
--I can't say excitement is
the only feeling I have,
--Guys, are you serious?
--Are you all idiots? Or just idiots?

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.700
but I still look forward to this!

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.790
"Planet Vilavurs
Day 4 of wandering in space"

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.500
Huh, this planet seems nice.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.870
Shouldn't we be a bit more cautious?

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.910
What-- What was that?

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.080
Over there!

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.660
Wow, it's big! Like a dragon!

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.250
If it attacks us, we're doomed.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.120
Um, I was thinking.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.790
Its head looks like a turtle.
Let's call it a Tur-Gon.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.910
Why are you so happy to see it?
Are you stupid or something?!

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:50.870
Stop being scared!
I'll catch one and eat it!

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:54.660
You sound like the first character
that dies in a horror movie.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.500
I can't stand it anymore!

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.450
Let's get off of this planet, and fast!

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.200
--Boo!
--Wow!

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.620
Wh-What?!

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:11.120
I've never heard you use
such a loud voice, Yunhua.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:16.950
"Thump thump"
Cut it out Aries, we're all connected
via helmet communicator!

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.660
"Thump thump"
Oops, sorry!

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.450
What's the deal?

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.120
So loud!

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.500
Um...

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.370
Seems like the broken communicator
is back in good order.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.580
Yes!

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.290
Zack was able to fix it up!

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.660
Maybe we should have kept it broken.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.620
Ha, ha!

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:41.290
Ah, that was supposed to be my job.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.750
This time, I'll do it.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.500
I'm going to be a truly reliable leader.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.500
We'll split up into three teams.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.540
Zack and Funicia, prepare the ship.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.620
Understood.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.830
Gotcha.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.580
Ulgar and Yunhua, load up the water.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.370
The rest of us will go foraging for food.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.290
No.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.700
What?!

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.580
I'm not doing anything dangerous.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:08.250
Well, of course there's some risk,
but I promise I'll be extra careful...

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.120
I don't trust you.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.290
What?!

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:15.040
Um, what kind of food
should we be looking for?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.370
Oh yeah, good question.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:22.330
Nuts are usually the safest and
most nutritious, berries are second.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:28.040
Mushrooms and red plants,
on the other hand, are risky, due to poisons.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.700
Impressive, Kanata!

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.080
You sound reliable for the first time!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.500
Ha, ha, ha! Follow me, friends!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.870
"Gloom"

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.750
So...

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.330
Which is a nut, and which is a berry?

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:48.290
How should I know?! I'm sorry, okay?!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.120
This is wonderful.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:55.660
The local flora and environment appear
similar to the Treepeel Spat system.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:59.450
We can expect species with
well-developed fibrovascular bundles!

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.450
I don't understand a word he said,
but I can tell he's more impressive!

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:06.080
Charce, you know a lot about plants!

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.580
Oh no, I'm just curious.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.660
Let's just grab whatever we can find.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.080
We can figure out if it's safe or not later.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.700
His instructions are getting vague.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.200
It won't attack, will it?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.660
Such large flying creatures
wouldn't fit in the deep forest.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.000
It's a space creature!

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.040
Of course. We're in a forest after all.

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.160
I just noticed, they're everywhere!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.700
They'd better not be dangerous!

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.620
There's no way to tell.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.830
Oh stop, Juliano.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.700
--Why is the hot one so crazy?!
Stop blending in so quickly!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.450
--Oh, you're a naughty one...
--Why is the hot one so crazy?!
Stop blending in so quickly!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.950
This stick totally looks like a sword!

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:13.580
Mine's a spear! I call it the Luca Javelin!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:17.620
What is up with the boys?
Is this just another field trip for you?!

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:28.330
This tree is fun.
It's like a trampoline!

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:31.910
The top side is grass-like.
Is this for photosynthesis?

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.540
Let's play sumo!

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.700
Why aren't any of you afraid
of the unknown?!

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:43.250
Why don't you join us, Quitterie? It's fun!

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.500
Hmph.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:52.620
It's like I'm the only one
seriously foraging out here.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.450
Here comes Quitterie.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:05.200
Interesting! A parachute-like structure,
to spread the seeds in the heavy fruit!

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.160
Stop analyzing calmly!

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.330
Cool, a star-shape.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.370
This is awesome.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:30.040
Everything here is completely new.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.250
Hey, we can't be too relaxed.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:38.160
Yeah, let's find some food.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.370
Hey, you suggested the sumo match!

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:07.450
Is something wrong, Zack?

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:08.700
Nothing.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.330
Looks like we got food and water.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.830
Yeah.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:22.120
Don't give up, and it'll work out.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.870
Right, tomorrow let's hunt animals!

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.870
No way!

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.330
It's fine.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:32.370
One swift stab of the Luca Javelin
will end the hunt super-fast!

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:35.700
But you left it on the trampoline tree.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.040
Oh, oops.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.950
Don't give up...

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.830
It's that ball!

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.080
Run!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.410
Run to the ship!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.160
What is that thing?!

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.660
Helmets on!

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.000
Which way is the ship?!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:06.830
Is it this way?!

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:08.200
No, it's this way!

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.870
Come on!

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.200
I remember that tree!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.200
This way!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.910
Get past that rock,
and we'll be out of the forest!

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.500
Aries, do you remember
all the scenery that you saw?

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.160
I have a photographic memory.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:48.250
What is that stupid sphere?!

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.370
I'm sick of this! I'm going home!

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.910
Why do I have to stay on this stupid planet?!

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.830
We're working on getting home!

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:59.750
Is it possible that the sphere
would take us back to McPa?

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:03.080
No, I don't think so.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.330
I saw the inside of the sphere--
it was space.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.580
We'd probably get dumped
back into outer space.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:13.410
This is the second time we saw it.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:16.370
Is it really a natural phenomenon?

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:21.700
I feel like we're getting caught up
in something really big and scary...

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.870
What?!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:31.200
He suddenly started eating!
He couldn't stand the silence!

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.500
We don't even know if it's edible yet!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:34.950
Is he stupid?!

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.830
Shut up. I'm hungry.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:45.000
Up in the mountains, the biggest enemies
were hunger and being alone with thoughts.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:50.750
Is help coming? There's no way of knowing.
It was driving me insane.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.410
You don't know what you don't know,
no matter how hard you think.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.000
Stating the obvious again...

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.000
But he has a point.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.870
For now, we just have to tackle
the issues in front of us to survive.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.450
So eat up! Captain's orders.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:13.080
Huh? What gives you the right
to boss us around? You're useless!

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.830
Charce is much better suited for leading!

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:21.540
Stop, Quitterie. Kanata, don't mind her.

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:28.290
If you're gonna act so bossy,
do something about the Tur-Gons or the ball!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:32.830
Fine then! I'll go and catch a Tur-Gon!

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:33.830
What?!

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:37.910
Then you'll have to admit I'm captain!

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:40.950
Kanata, don't be so easily taunted.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.750
I am not!

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.040
You've gone too far, Quitterie.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.250
Hmph.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.790
You haven't changed
from when we were little.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:57.160
How many friends have you lost that way?

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:58.540
Whatever!

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.790
I don't need friends!

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:05.160
None of these people are friends anyway!

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.200
Quitterie...

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.330
Can't we all get along?

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.160
Stop being a smart mouth!
You're not even my real sister!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.870
Quitterie!

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.790
Well, that fell apart.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.410
How far did Quitterie go?

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.330
Don't worry, she's not a child.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:43.330
Zack, you seem to know Quitterie well.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:45.580
Yes. We're childhood friends.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:49.370
I see. Has she always been like that?

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:50.790
Yes.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:56.040
She has no father, and her mother
is a busy doctor who is never around.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:12:00.700
She was practically raised by caretakers
and staff, which made her selfish.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.080
She doesn't know how to deal with people.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:07.200
She also couldn't figure out how
to deal with suddenly having a sister.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.750
Suddenly?

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:15.080
Funi is from an orphanage,
and Quitterie's mother brought her in.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.660
I like Quitterie.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.120
I didn't have any siblings or friends.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:24.080
I'm happy to have
a pretty sister like Quitterie.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.080
Huh? An adoption?!

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:31.330
What do you mean, Mom?!

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:36.000
I mean exactly that. A friend of mine
passed away and left her daughter.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.500
I've decided to bring her into the family.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.080
Take care of her.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.950
Take care? Me?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.910
You don't take care of children.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.040
You don't even love your own child.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:00.040
Why have more?

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.080
I'm Funicia.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:06.160
Don't get close to me.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.580
Nobody taught me how to love.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.830
Hmm? Where's Funi?

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:15.500
What? Where?

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:18.410
We were concentrating too
much on finding Quitterie.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:20.410
Over here!

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:23.330
Oh, it's the trampoline tree!

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:26.950
There's a pretty flower here!

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.660
What's going on?!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.700
The trampoline tree grew?!

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.040
Funi!

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.540
Quitterie!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.160
Funicia!

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:52.750
Quitterie!

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.160
Funicia!

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.450
Hold on! I'm coming!

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:12.620
If it's reacting to the sunlight,
it should come back down at night...

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.370
We have to wait for that?!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.450
We're too high up to build a bridge...

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:24.950
A Tur-Gon!

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.450
It's trying to get Funi!

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.660
Funicia!

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.080
Kanata!

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.830
Kanata?!

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:46.790
Can I reach that closest footing...?

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.910
Is he going to jump,
without the anti-gravity shoes?

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.450
When things seem hopeless...

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:56.120
...act tough!

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.620
--He made it!
--Good!

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:04.870
Awesome!

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:12.450
Isn't he scared of dying?
That drop is totally lethal. Who is he?

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:15.870
Kanata Hoshijima... I remember!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.620
I saw a news article about him.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:26.450
He's a decathlete, the sport where
you run, jump, and throw, all by yourself.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.500
No wonder he's so athletic.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:33.160
That alone doesn't explain why
he can make that jump.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:38.660
Kanata has the ability to
risk his life for his friends.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.120
Yes!

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.290
Good, Kanata!

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.750
Just one more!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:50.000
Just wait, Funi...

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.950
He's exhausted...

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:57.200
Of course. He made so many consecutive
jumps under such intense pressure.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.540
I'm going.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.290
Hey, Quitterie!

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.500
Funi!

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.750
No!

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:11.580
--No!
--We can't let it fly away with her!

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.660
I can't reach it from here!

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.000
Isn't there any way?!

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.290
Is there...?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.370
That's the...

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.040
Luca Javelin!

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.580
What?!

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:30.250
Javelin throw!

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:34.200
Go! Kanata!

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.160
He did it!

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.250
He got it!

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.330
Funi's okay too!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.620
Phew, I'm exhausted.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:56.790
Just wait, Funi.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:02.370
Just like when he saved me.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:07.540
He came flying through space, and said...

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.620
"You did well."

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.000
You...

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.080
...did...

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.580
Whoa...

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:18.750
No!

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:28.080
What?!

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:31.790
Just in time.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:35.700
He's too confident.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.040
You did well.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.500
Thanks!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.200
Funicia!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.540
I'm sorry! It's all my fault!

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:56.910
No, it's my fault.
I'm sorry I went up the tree.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:18:00.290
I saw a flower like yours,
so I wanted to get it...

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.790
A flower?

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.330
Is this...?

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:14.580
I'm sorry, Funi...

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.950
Funi.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:30.950
Thank you, Kanata.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:32.120
Huh?

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:38.080
I apologize for how I was back there.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:44.040
No, I apologize for how
I've been this whole time.

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.870
This whole time...

00:18:45.870 --> 00:18:49.790
I couldn't be honest.

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:53.870
I didn't know how to deal with friends...

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:00.370
You can start being honest from now.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.540
To your family, and your friends.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.830
You shouldn't be the one talking.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.080
What?!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.290
Not honest...

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.160
Hmph!

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.950
That was quite impressive, Kanata!

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:20.160
I mean the athletics were amazing,
but the nerves of steel are ridiculous!

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.160
Do you have like holes in your body
to grease up your metal parts?!

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.750
Is that really a compliment?!

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:29.790
I didn't know you were a decathlete.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:35.950
It's not like my job or anything,
but my dad trained me.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:43.580
My dad used to be a world-class athlete,
but he had to retire early from an injury.

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:51.330
He more or less forced his dream on me,
and I always wanted to run away.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:58.330
When I met my teacher in middle school,
I got interested in space exploration.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:01.700
I was finally free from my dad.

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:05.450
Then we got lost in the mountains.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:12.790
If only I had more stamina, more courage...

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:16.290
Maybe I could have done more,

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:19.200
and maybe my teacher would be alive.

00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:24.120
I begged my dad to train me again.

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:30.910
I don't intend on competing, though.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:36.000
I'm not taking over my dad's dream.
I'm taking over my teacher's.

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.620
I also intend on going into space research.

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:47.250
I'll join you on your ship, Kanata.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:51.500
Yes, I'd like to be there too.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:55.540
That's great! Please lead this team as well.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.660
Hold on a sec.

00:20:57.660 --> 00:21:00.160
I'm not fit to be captain.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:06.120
I took a stupid risk all on my own.
If Quitterie didn't help me, I'd be dead.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:08.950
Like Quitterie said, Charce should be...

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:13.790
Not many people can make and execute
critical decisions without hesitation.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:18.160
Not like you. Everyone agrees.

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:27.830
I can be your second in command.

00:21:27.830 --> 00:21:29.870
You should be captain.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:35.830
All right then. Thanks everyone!

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.120
Don't mention it!

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:39.410
Awaiting instructions!

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:40.410
Well then!

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:43.370
Let's haul this back to the ship.

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:44.790
What?!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:54.250
Seriously, Tur-Gon meat is delicious!

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:57.080
I can just eat this for the rest of my life!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.200
Yes!

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.120
Delicious!

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:05.000
But we may need to balance
our diet over the next 20 days.

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:09.870
About that... I've gathered some junk
parts from around the ship,

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:11.660
and assembled an edibility tester.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.580
This guy is amazing.

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:16.250
For example, with this berry...

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:20.120
Yummy.

00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:21.950
The display design is rather
approachable, isn't it?!

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:25.200
Did you record your own voice for this?

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:34.950
What's wrong, Aries...?

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:38.410
I'm sorry, that was just very funny.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:44.250
This might be inappropriate,
but I'm starting to enjoy this situation.

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:49.250
I lived out in the country,
and didn't have many friends.

00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:54.160
So I'm glad to be friends with all of you.

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.500
Team B5, camp log.

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:08.160
We were able to leave
Planet Vilavurs in two full days.

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:12.370
Also, we all got closer to each other!

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:22.040
Kanata, there's something I
want to discuss, just with you.

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:25.200
The communicator was
intentionally destroyed?!

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:26.870
What does that mean?!

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:32.870
I took a closer look. The missing parts
appear to have been cut out,

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:36.200
and the cuts seem very new.

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:38.950
So, you mean...

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:43.000
One of the people on
this ship is behind this.
